    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Explore the Pokemon Database\r\n\r\nSkim the official Pokémon API documentation in `documentation.md`. Then look at the JSON response for a single Pokémon in `pokemon.json` to figure out how the data is structured. \r\n\r\nUse AI Tutor to help you modify your code to display different stats (like \"order\" or \"base species\").\r\n\r\n_Hint: You can upload files like `pokemon.json` to use when prompting AI Tutor._\r\n\r\n:::details [Not sure how to modify the code?] \r\n\r\nTry one of the following prompts:\r\n\r\n- In the file `pokemon.json`, how do I find the Pokemon's name?\r\n- How do I change the code to display \"base\\_experience\" as a percentage?\r\n- What is the difference between \"abilities\" and \"forms\" in this data?\r\n:::",
